  "entry": "code/index.html",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A browser tool that runs entirely on the user's computer. It turns a gel photo into per-lane intensity profiles, calibrates them against a DNA ladder to estimate band sizes, quantifies bands, checks bands against expected digest/PCR fragments, and exports CSV, SVG, PNG, HTML report and project JSON. Data used in the run: stock. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
